    "productionAccepted": false,
    "hypothesis": "Remove per-strip copying of already prepared vertical weights. Shared geometry returns an exact readonly result-footer view only when all publications/repairs in that strip end before its protected footer; other prepared boundary strips keep a copy, and unprepared tails retain the original stack-built Kernel path.",
    "intendedEndState": "One geometry read/preparation path shared by small/wide column drivers, without another cache/session or general pixel-loop abstraction. Preserve bit-identical weight doubles, counts/first/normalizer, Multiply/Add and repair order. No new owned capacity or weaker numerical policy.",
    "lifetime": "Footer initialized before strips; borrowed view stays inside current synchronous row. Prove column+length<=PrefixColumns before borrowing, so every pair/single/repair write is disjoint from that footer. Existing result owner and4KiB reservation outlive all users; release/failure/cancellation paths unchanged. Cache rows and geometry footer are already disjoint. No returned object retains the view.",
    "boundaryCounterexample": {
      "source": [
        324,
        128
      ],
      "output": [
        144,
        64
      ],
      "depth": 16,
      "taps": [
        10,
        9
      ],
      "rowSlots": 10,
      "suffixStrip": 6,
      "geometryPrefixColumns": 132,
      "resultCachePrefixColumns": 64,
      "lastPreparedColumn": 130,
      "weightsOffsetBytes": 1072,
      "stripOutputEndBytes": 1088,
      "overlapBytes": 16,
      "consequence": "Testing only tile<PrefixColumns is insufficient for a borrowed view. The out-of-phase final prepared suffix strip can overwrite footer weights; a subsequent exact repair can still read them. Keep a copy for this boundary rather than weakening the exact repair contract."
    },
    "potentialSetback": "Borrowed heap views can change JIT alias/bounds behavior despite removing copy work. Preserve complete-operation adverse/uncertain results and revise or abandon if useful elapsed gains/simplification do not materialize. No allocation reduction is assumed; all stack capacity remains admitted.",
    "checks": "Prepared exact-bit views, crossing-strip copy, retired-footer direct construction, cancellation/root lifetime, existing frozen small/wide byte/word and exact2.25 alias boundary. Existing wide-byte complete short first, small affected generalization if useful; independent confirmation and W/L full/live/scalar/sameactualpackage only at coherent acceptance."
  },
